# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 2: a named Structure's statements are checked whether or not it is
# executed -- here it is not, and `n: n + g` reads g, a field of the unit, not of Counter: this slice
# walks the Structure's own number fields.  Before, the statement was set aside unchecked.
size_t: g 2U
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + g
return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
